   "text": "A curve has equation $y = \\dfrac{4x^3 - 3}{2\\sqrt{x}}$, where $x > 0$.\n\nFind $\\dfrac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}$. Write your answer as a sum of terms, where each term is a constant times a power of $x$. (3)",
   "command": "find",
   "skills": [
    "differentiate-polynomials"
   ],
   "mark_scheme": [
    {
     "code": "M1",
     "for": "Splits the fraction into two separate powers of $x$, e.g. $2x^{5/2} - \\tfrac{3}{2}x^{-1/2}$ (the coefficients may be wrong), and then differentiates, lowering the index of at least one of these terms by 1",
     "notes": "Differentiating the numerator and the denominator separately, or differentiating before writing $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}$ as $x^{-1/2}$, gets M0. A correct quotient rule attempt also earns this mark."
    },
    {
